1
00:01:13,820 --> 00:01:15,570
Bye. - Later.

2
00:02:05,870 --> 00:02:09,590
This is a customer announcement. The store will be closing in five minutes.

3
00:02:09,670 --> 00:02:10,710
Thank you.

4
00:02:15,180 --> 00:02:16,220
Oi!

5
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:47,040
Wilson?

6
00:02:48,670 --> 00:02:50,840
Wilson, I've got the lottery money.

7
00:02:52,380 --> 00:02:53,550
Wilson?

8
00:02:54,880 --> 00:02:56,380
You there?

9
00:02:58,470 --> 00:03:00,970
I can't hang about cause they're closing the shop.

10
00:03:02,680 --> 00:03:03,850
Wilson?

11
00:03:04,770 --> 00:03:06,180
Oh, come on.

12
00:03:09,690 --> 00:03:10,900
Hello?

13
00:03:14,230 --> 00:03:16,280
Hello? Wilson, it's Rose.

14
00:03:19,450 --> 00:03:20,660
Hello?

15
00:03:22,120 --> 00:03:23,740
W... Wilson?

16
00:03:49,810 --> 00:03:51,150
Wilson?

17
00:04:00,860 --> 00:04:02,160
Wilson?

18
00:04:19,840 --> 00:04:21,260
You're kidding me!

19
00:04:27,770 --> 00:04:29,980
Is there someone mucking about?

20
00:04:40,780 --> 00:04:42,240
Who is it?

21
00:05:00,050 --> 00:05:02,050
You got me. Very funny.

22
00:05:05,260 --> 00:05:07,140
Right, I've got the joke!

23
00:05:07,220 --> 00:05:10,810
Whose idea was this? Is it Derek's?

24
00:05:10,890 --> 00:05:12,350
Is it?

25
00:05:13,770 --> 00:05:15,560
Derek, is this you?

26
00:05:39,500 --> 00:05:40,960
Run!

27
00:06:10,450 --> 00:06:14,040
You pulled his arm off! - Yep, plastic.

28
00:06:14,290 --> 00:06:17,130
Very clever, nice trick. Who are they then, students?

29
00:06:17,210 --> 00:06:20,090
Is this a student thing or what? - Why would they be students?

30
00:06:20,170 --> 00:06:21,170
I don't know!

31
00:06:21,250 --> 00:06:22,960
Well you said it. Why students?

32
00:06:23,050 --> 00:06:28,300
Cause... To get that many people dressed up and being silly they've got to be students.

33
00:06:28,390 --> 00:06:30,560
That makes sense, well done. - Thanks.

34
00:06:30,640 --> 00:06:31,640
They're not students.

35
00:06:31,720 --> 00:06:33,850
Whoever they are, when Wilson finds them he's gonna call the police.

36
00:06:33,930 --> 00:06:36,020
Who's Wilson? - Chief electrician.

37
00:06:36,100 --> 00:06:37,600
Wilson's dead.

38
00:06:39,150 --> 00:06:41,980
That's just not funny, that's sick! - Hold on, mind your eyes.

39
00:06:42,280 --> 00:06:43,940
I've had enough of this, now.

40
00:06:44,820 --> 00:06:48,160
Who are you, then? Who's that lot down there?

41
00:06:48,240 --> 00:06:50,280
I said who are they?

42
00:06:50,370 --> 00:06:53,500
Living plastic. Living plastic creatures.

43
00:06:53,580 --> 00:06:55,870
They're being controlled by a relay device from the roof

44
00:06:55,960 --> 00:06:58,630
which would be a great big problem if I didn't have this.

45
00:06:58,710 --> 00:07:01,550
So, I'm gonna go upstairs and blow it up.

46
00:07:01,630 --> 00:07:04,260
And I might well die in the process but don't worry about me, no.

47
00:07:04,340 --> 00:07:07,340
You go home. Go on, go have your lovely beans on toast.

48
00:07:07,430 --> 00:07:10,550
Don't tell anyone about this cause if you do you'll get them killed.

49
00:07:14,100 --> 00:07:15,640
I'm the Doctor, by the way, what's your name?

50
00:07:15,730 --> 00:07:17,440
Rose. - Nice to meet you Rose.

51
00:07:17,520 --> 00:07:19,150
Run for your life!

52
00:08:13,660 --> 00:08:18,330
The whole of Central London has been closed off as police investigate the fire.

53
00:08:18,460 --> 00:08:19,370
Early reports indicate...

54
00:08:19,460 --> 00:08:24,040
I know, it's on the telly! It's everywhere! She's lucky to be alive.

55
00:08:24,130 --> 00:08:27,090
Honestly, it's aged her. Skin like an old Bible.

56
00:08:27,170 --> 00:08:29,630
Walking in here, you'd think I was her daughter.

57
00:08:29,720 --> 00:08:31,220
Oh, and here's himself.

58
00:08:31,760 --> 00:08:33,640
I've been phoning your mobile! You could have been dead!

59
00:08:33,720 --> 00:08:36,430
It's on the news and everything! I can't believe that your shop went up!

60
00:08:36,510 --> 00:08:39,640
I'm alright, honestly, I'm fine! Don't make a fuss.

61
00:08:39,730 --> 00:08:41,940
But what happened? - I don't know.

62
00:08:42,020 --> 00:08:43,230
What was it though, what caused it?

63
00:08:43,310 --> 00:08:45,730
I wasn't in the shop. I was outside, didn't see anything.

64
00:08:45,820 --> 00:08:49,860
It's Debbie on the end. She knows a man on the Mirror, 500 quid for an interview!

65
00:08:49,950 --> 00:08:51,610
Oh, that's brilliant, give it here.

66
00:08:54,490 --> 00:08:57,290
Well you've got to find some way of making money, your job's kaput

67
00:08:57,370 --> 00:08:59,660
and I'm not bailing you out.

68
00:09:01,080 --> 00:09:03,040
Bev! She's alive!

69
00:09:03,120 --> 00:09:07,840
I've told her, sue for compensation! She was within seconds of death...

70
00:09:07,920 --> 00:09:10,670
What are you drinking, tea? Nah nah, that's no good, that's no good.

71
00:09:10,760 --> 00:09:12,180
You're in shock, you need something stronger.

72
00:09:12,260 --> 00:09:13,390
I'm alright. - Now come on.

73
00:09:13,470 --> 00:09:15,550
You deserve a proper drink. We're going down the pub, you and me.

74
00:09:15,640 --> 00:09:18,010
My treat. How about it? - Is there a match on?

75
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:21,140
No, no, I'm just thinking about you babe.

76
00:09:21,230 --> 00:09:23,020
There's a match on, ain't there?

77
00:09:23,100 --> 00:09:25,270
Well that's not the point, but we could catch the last five minutes.

78
00:09:25,360 --> 00:09:28,280
Go on, then. I'm fine, really. Go.

79
00:09:28,360 --> 00:09:30,110
Get rid of that.

80
00:09:39,240 --> 00:09:40,660
Bye-bye! - Bye!

81
00:09:40,750 --> 00:09:42,250
Aaaggghhh!

82
00:09:42,330 --> 00:09:47,000
Fire then spread throughout the store. Fifteen fire crews are attendant

83
00:09:47,090 --> 00:09:50,210
though it's thought there is very little chance of saving the infrastructure.

84
00:10:19,740 --> 00:10:24,870
There's no point in getting up, sweetheart. You've no job to go to.

85
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:29,960
There's Finch's.

86
00:10:31,250 --> 00:10:35,010
You could try them, they've always got jobs. - Oh, great, the butcher's.

87
00:10:35,090 --> 00:10:38,390
Well it might do you good. That shop was giving you airs and graces.

88
00:10:38,470 --> 00:10:43,060
And I'm not joking about compensation. You've had genuine shock and trauma.

89
00:10:43,140 --> 00:10:46,560
Arianna got 2,000 quid off the council just cause the old man behind the desk

90
00:10:46,650 --> 00:10:48,560
said she looked Greek!

91
00:10:48,650 --> 00:10:53,360
I know she is Greek, but that's not the point. It was a valid claim.

92
00:10:57,410 --> 00:11:00,580
Mum, you're such a liar! I told you to nail the cat-flap down.

93
00:11:00,660 --> 00:11:01,830
We're gonna get strays!

94
00:11:01,910 --> 00:11:05,210
I did it weeks back. - Nah, you thought about it.

95
00:11:21,970 --> 00:11:23,890
What are you doing here? - I live here.

96
00:11:23,970 --> 00:11:26,480
Well what do you do that for? - Cause I do!

97
00:11:26,560 --> 00:11:28,940
I'm only home cause someone blew up my job!

98
00:11:29,020 --> 00:11:31,820
I must have the wrong signal. You're not plastic, are you?

99
00:11:31,900 --> 00:11:33,730
Nope, bonehead. Bye then.

100
00:11:33,820 --> 00:11:35,780
You, inside, right now.

101
00:11:35,860 --> 00:11:37,780
Who is it?

102
00:11:38,910 --> 00:11:42,330
It's about last night. He's part of the inquiry. Give us ten minutes.

103
00:11:42,410 --> 00:11:44,490
She deserves compensation!

104
00:11:44,580 --> 00:11:46,660
Oh, we're talking millions.

105
00:11:47,410 --> 00:11:51,130
Um... I'm in my dressing gown.

106
00:11:51,210 --> 00:11:52,790
Yes, you are.

107
00:11:53,880 --> 00:11:56,720
There's a strange man in my bedroom.

108
00:11:56,800 --> 00:11:58,340
Yes, there is.

109
00:12:00,010 --> 00:12:02,050
Well, anything could happen.

110
00:12:03,510 --> 00:12:04,970
No.

111
00:12:08,480 --> 00:12:10,650
Don't mind the mess. Do you want a coffee?

112
00:12:10,730 --> 00:12:12,520
Might as well, thanks, just milk.

113
00:12:13,310 --> 00:12:15,980
We should go to the police. Seriously.

114
00:12:16,070 --> 00:12:18,400
That won't last, he's gay and she's an alien.

115
00:12:18,490 --> 00:12:21,660
I'm not blaming you, even if it was some sort of joke that just...

116
00:12:21,740 --> 00:12:23,320
Hm. Sad ending.

117
00:12:24,120 --> 00:12:27,750
It said on the news they found a body. - "Rose Tyler."

118
00:12:28,710 --> 00:12:31,540
Ah, could've been worse. Look at the ears!

119
00:12:31,620 --> 00:12:35,420
All the same, he was nice. He was a nice bloke. - ♪ Luck be a lady ♪

120
00:12:35,500 --> 00:12:39,920
Anyway, if we are gonna go to the police, I wanna know what I'm saying.

121
00:12:40,010 --> 00:12:41,970
I want you to explain everything. - Maybe not.

122
00:12:43,090 --> 00:12:44,640
What's that then?

123
00:12:45,970 --> 00:12:46,890
Have you got a cat?

124
00:12:46,970 --> 00:12:48,430
No.

125
00:12:49,520 --> 00:12:54,060
We did have, but we just get strays. They come in off the estate.

126
00:12:59,070 --> 00:13:01,070
I told Mickey to chuck that out.

127
00:13:01,150 --> 00:13:04,700
You're all the same. Give a man a plastic hand...

128
00:13:04,780 --> 00:13:08,370
Anyway, I don't even know your name. Doctor, what what it?

129
00:13:10,160 --> 00:13:11,160
Aah!

130
00:13:37,230 --> 00:13:38,610
It's all right, I've stopped it.

131
00:13:38,690 --> 00:13:42,280
There you go, you see? Armless! - Do you think?

132
00:13:42,570 --> 00:13:43,610
Ow!

133
00:13:44,820 --> 00:13:47,030
Hold on a minute, you can't just go swanning off.

134
00:13:47,120 --> 00:13:49,870
I can. Here I am. This is me, swanning off. See ya!

135
00:13:49,950 --> 00:13:52,370
But that arm was moving, it tried to kill me!

136
00:13:52,460 --> 00:13:53,920
Ten out of ten for observation.

137
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:56,040
You can't just walk away, that's not fair!

138
00:13:56,130 --> 00:13:59,210
You've got to tell me what's going on. - No, I don't.

139
00:14:02,170 --> 00:14:05,930
All right then, I'll go to the police. I'll tell everyone.

140
00:14:06,010 --> 00:14:10,180
You said if I did that I'd get people killed. So, your choice.

141
00:14:10,270 --> 00:14:12,560
Tell me or I'll start talking.

142
00:14:12,680 --> 00:14:14,640
Is that supposed to sound tough?

143
00:14:14,730 --> 00:14:16,980
Sort of. - Doesn't work.

144
00:14:17,440 --> 00:14:19,940
Who are you? - I told you, the Doctor.

145
00:14:20,020 --> 00:14:21,650
Yeah, but Doctor what?

146
00:14:21,730 --> 00:14:23,740
Just the Doctor. - The Doctor?

147
00:14:23,820 --> 00:14:24,990
Hello!

148
00:14:26,320 --> 00:14:28,320
Is that supposed to sound impressive?

149
00:14:28,450 --> 00:14:29,870
Sort of.

150
00:14:30,370 --> 00:14:34,290
Come on then, you can tell me. I've seen enough.

151
00:14:35,160 --> 00:14:39,250
Are you the police? - No! I was just... Passing through.

152
00:14:39,340 --> 00:14:40,630
I'm a long way from home.

153
00:14:40,710 --> 00:14:44,340
But what have I done wrong? How come those plastic things keep coming after me?

154
00:14:44,420 --> 00:14:46,970
Oh, suddenly the entire world revolves around you.

155
00:14:47,050 --> 00:14:49,350
You were just an accident. You got in the way, that's all.

156
00:14:49,430 --> 00:14:52,020
It tried to kill me! - It was after me, not you!

157
00:14:52,100 --> 00:14:54,640
Last night, in the shop, I was there, you blundered in,

158
00:14:54,730 --> 00:14:57,810
almost ruined the whole thing. This morning, I was tracking it down,

159
00:14:57,900 --> 00:14:59,560
it was tracking me down.

160
00:14:59,650 --> 00:15:01,940
The only reason it fixed on you is cause you've met me.

161
00:15:02,030 --> 00:15:06,280
So what you're saying is, the entire world revolves around you?

162
00:15:06,360 --> 00:15:08,530
Sort of, yeah. - You're full of it!

163
00:15:08,620 --> 00:15:10,200
Sort of, yeah.

164
00:15:10,700 --> 00:15:11,410
But...

165
00:15:11,580 --> 00:15:14,290
All this plastic stuff, who else knows about it?

166
00:15:14,370 --> 00:15:15,620
No-one.

167
00:15:15,910 --> 00:15:17,710
What, you're on your own?

168
00:15:18,170 --> 00:15:21,210
Well, who else is there? I mean, you lot, all you do is eat chips, go to bed

169
00:15:21,290 --> 00:15:25,090
and watch telly! While all the time, underneath you, there's a war going on.

170
00:15:26,630 --> 00:15:29,680
Okay. Start from the beginning.

171
00:15:31,390 --> 00:15:33,140
I mean, if we're gonna go with the living plastic,

172
00:15:33,220 --> 00:15:36,140
and I don't even believe that, but if we do,

173
00:15:36,230 --> 00:15:37,770
how did you kill it?

174
00:15:37,850 --> 00:15:41,810
The thing controlling it projects life into the arm. I cut off the signal. There.

175
00:15:41,900 --> 00:15:45,190
So, that's radio control? - Thought control.

176
00:15:46,240 --> 00:15:48,320
You all right? - Yeah.

177
00:15:48,660 --> 00:15:51,070
So who's controlling it then? - Long story.

178
00:15:51,160 --> 00:15:56,370
But what's it all for? I mean, shop window dummies, what's that about?

179
00:15:56,580 --> 00:15:59,670
Is someone trying to take over Britain's shops?

180
00:15:59,750 --> 00:16:00,920
No.

181
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:04,590
Well, no. - It's not a price war.

182
00:16:06,630 --> 00:16:10,010
They want to overthrow the human race and destroy you.

183
00:16:10,340 --> 00:16:12,050
Do you believe me? - No.

184
00:16:12,140 --> 00:16:13,810
But you're still listening.

185
00:16:15,140 --> 00:16:17,560
Really, though, Doctor... Tell me.

186
00:16:17,640 --> 00:16:19,770
Who are you?

187
00:16:24,270 --> 00:16:28,610
Do you know like we were saying? About the Earth revolving?

188
00:16:30,320 --> 00:16:32,280
It's like when you were a kid.

189
00:16:32,370 --> 00:16:34,530
The first time they tell you the world's turning

190
00:16:34,620 --> 00:16:39,660
and you can't quite believe it cause it looks like everything's standing still.

191
00:16:41,540 --> 00:16:43,790
I can feel it.

192
00:16:45,960 --> 00:16:47,800
The turn of the Earth.

193
00:16:48,380 --> 00:16:51,840
The ground beneath our feet is spinning at 1,000 miles an hour

194
00:16:51,930 --> 00:16:56,350
and the entire planet is hurtling round the sun at 67,000 miles an hour.

195
00:16:56,430 --> 00:17:00,520
I can feel it. We're falling through Space, you and me.

196
00:17:00,600 --> 00:17:04,690
Clinging to the skin of this tiny little world, and if we let go...

197
00:17:07,980 --> 00:17:12,320
That's who I am. Now forget me, Rose Tyler.

198
00:17:13,490 --> 00:17:15,370
Go home.

199
00:18:18,140 --> 00:18:21,270
Hey, here's my woman! Kit off. Oh, shut up.

200
00:18:23,230 --> 00:18:26,020
Coffee? - Yeah, only if you wash the mug.

201
00:18:26,100 --> 00:18:28,520
And I don't mean rinse, I mean wash. Can I use your computer?

202
00:18:28,610 --> 00:18:32,030
Yeah. Any excuse to get in the bedroom.

203
00:18:32,820 --> 00:18:35,280
Don't read my e-mails!

204
00:19:18,530 --> 00:19:20,450
You're not coming in!

205
00:19:21,200 --> 00:19:23,240
He's safe, he's got a wife and kids.

206
00:19:23,330 --> 00:19:25,160
Yeah, who told you that? He did!

207
00:19:25,250 --> 00:19:28,830
That's exactly what an internet lunatic murderer would say.

208
00:19:52,610 --> 00:19:56,860
Um, hello, I've come to see Clive. We've been e-mailing.

209
00:19:56,940 --> 00:20:00,530
Dad! It's one of your nutters.

210
00:20:03,200 --> 00:20:07,540
Sorry, hello! You must be Rose. I'm Clive. Obviously.

211
00:20:07,620 --> 00:20:09,960
I'd better tell you now. My boyfriend's waiting in the car

212
00:20:10,040 --> 00:20:11,670
just in case you're going to kill me.

213
00:20:11,750 --> 00:20:14,590
No, good point! No murders!

214
00:20:14,670 --> 00:20:17,920
Who is it? - Oh, it's something to do with the Doctor.

215
00:20:18,010 --> 00:20:21,720
She's been reading the website. Please come through, I'm in the shed.

216
00:20:22,760 --> 00:20:23,970
She?

217
00:20:24,310 --> 00:20:28,480
She's read a website about the Doctor? She's a she?

218
00:20:32,770 --> 00:20:35,820
A lot of this stuff is quite sensitive. I couldn't just send it to you.

219
00:20:35,900 --> 00:20:39,150
People might intercept it, if you know what I mean.

220
00:20:39,490 --> 00:20:42,620
If you dig deep enough and keep a lively mind,

221
00:20:42,700 --> 00:20:45,410
this Doctor keeps cropping up all over the place.

222
00:20:45,490 --> 00:20:50,040
Political diaries, conspiracy theories, even ghost stories.

223
00:20:50,120 --> 00:20:56,090
No first name, no last name, just the Doctor. Always the Doctor.

224
00:20:56,170 --> 00:20:59,090
And the title seems to be passed down from father to son.

225
00:20:59,170 --> 00:21:00,800
It appears to be an inheritance.

226
00:21:00,880 --> 00:21:03,760
That's your Doctor there, isn't it? - Yeah.

227
00:21:03,840 --> 00:21:07,390
I tracked it down to the Washington Public Archive, just last year.

228
00:21:07,470 --> 00:21:11,980
The online photo's enhanced, but if we look at the original...

229
00:21:24,030 --> 00:21:29,830
November the 22nd 1963. The assassination of President Kennedy. You see?

230
00:21:31,870 --> 00:21:33,670
Must be his father.

231
00:21:33,750 --> 00:21:35,540
Going further back...

232
00:21:35,630 --> 00:21:37,920
April 1912.

233
00:21:39,130 --> 00:21:44,010
This is a photograph of the Daniels family of Southampton, and friend.

234
00:21:44,090 --> 00:21:46,850
This was taken the day before they were due to sail for the new world.

235
00:21:46,930 --> 00:21:48,390
On the Titanic.

236
00:21:48,470 --> 00:21:52,350
And for some unknown reason, they cancelled the trip and survived.

237
00:21:52,440 --> 00:21:55,020
And here we are...

238
00:21:55,730 --> 00:21:58,440
1883, another Doctor.

239
00:21:58,520 --> 00:22:02,490
Look, the same lineage. He's identical!

240
00:22:02,570 --> 00:22:04,280
This one washed up on the coast of Sumatra,

241
00:22:04,360 --> 00:22:07,490
on the very night the Krakatoa exploded.

242
00:22:07,910 --> 00:22:11,000
The Doctor is a legend, woven throughout history.

243
00:22:11,080 --> 00:22:13,500
When disaster comes, he's there.

244
00:22:13,580 --> 00:22:17,590
He brings the storm in his wake and has one constant companion.

245
00:22:17,670 --> 00:22:19,300
Who's that?

246
00:22:19,710 --> 00:22:21,460
Death.

247
00:22:44,030 --> 00:22:47,660
If the Doctor's back, if you've seen him, Rose,

248
00:22:47,740 --> 00:22:50,490
then one thing is for certain.

249
00:22:50,580 --> 00:22:52,790
We're all in danger.

250
00:23:28,030 --> 00:23:29,200
Come on then!

251
00:23:29,280 --> 00:23:33,700
If he singled you out, if the Doctor's making house calls...

252
00:23:36,370 --> 00:23:38,370
Then God help you.

253
00:24:21,750 --> 00:24:23,340
But... Who is he?

254
00:24:23,420 --> 00:24:25,210
Who do you think he is?

255
00:24:25,300 --> 00:24:27,970
I think he's the same man.

256
00:24:28,050 --> 00:24:30,300
I think he's immortal.

257
00:24:31,890 --> 00:24:35,720
I think he's an alien from another world.

258
00:24:37,350 --> 00:24:39,520
All right, he's a nutter. Off his head.

259
00:24:39,600 --> 00:24:44,110
Complete online conspiracy freak. You win!

260
00:24:45,320 --> 00:24:48,190
What are we going to do tonight? I fancy a pizza.

261
00:24:48,280 --> 00:24:50,280
Pizza! Puh-puh-puh.

262
00:24:51,200 --> 00:24:53,320
Pizza! - Or Chinese.

263
00:24:53,410 --> 00:24:55,700
Pizza!

264
00:25:06,340 --> 00:25:08,130
Do you think I should try the hospital?

265
00:25:08,210 --> 00:25:11,090
Suki said they had jobs going in the canteen.

266
00:25:11,880 --> 00:25:15,800
Is that it then, dishing out chips?

267
00:25:15,890 --> 00:25:18,850
I could do A-levels. I dunno.

268
00:25:18,930 --> 00:25:21,440
It's all Jimmy Stones's fault.

269
00:25:21,520 --> 00:25:24,360
I only left school cause of him and look where he ended up.

270
00:25:24,440 --> 00:25:26,270
What do you think?

271
00:25:26,360 --> 00:25:28,070
So where did you meet this Doctor?

272
00:25:28,150 --> 00:25:30,070
Oh, I'm sorry, was I talking about me for a second?

273
00:25:30,150 --> 00:25:32,700
Cause I reckon it all started back at the shop, am I right?

274
00:25:32,780 --> 00:25:35,240
Was he something to do with that? - No.

275
00:25:35,320 --> 00:25:37,030
Come on.

276
00:25:37,870 --> 00:25:39,540
Sort of.

277
00:25:40,200 --> 00:25:42,540
What was he doing there? - I'm not going on about it, Mickey.

278
00:25:42,620 --> 00:25:44,630
Really, I'm not, because...

279
00:25:44,710 --> 00:25:47,380
I know it sounds daft, but...

280
00:25:47,460 --> 00:25:50,590
I don't think he's safe. He's dangerous.

281
00:25:50,670 --> 00:25:52,260
But you can trust me, sweetheart.

282
00:25:52,340 --> 00:25:55,430
Babe, darling, sugar, babe, sugar.

283
00:25:55,510 --> 00:25:56,930
You can tell me anything.

284
00:25:57,010 --> 00:26:00,680
Tell me about the Doctor and what he's planning and I can help you, Rose.

285
00:26:00,770 --> 00:26:02,560
Because that's all I really want to do, sweetheart.

286
00:26:02,640 --> 00:26:05,020
Sugar, darling, babe, babe, sugar, sweetheart.

287
00:26:05,100 --> 00:26:06,940
What are you doing that for?

288
00:26:07,020 --> 00:26:09,320
Your champagne. - We didn't order any champagne.

289
00:26:09,400 --> 00:26:10,990
Where's the Doctor?

290
00:26:11,070 --> 00:26:12,530
Madam, your champagne.

291
00:26:13,490 --> 00:26:16,160
It's... It's not ours. Mickey, what is it, what's wrong?

292
00:26:16,240 --> 00:26:18,700
I need know out how much he knows, so where is he?

293
00:26:18,780 --> 00:26:23,000
Doesn't anybody want this champagne? - Look, we didn't order...

294
00:26:23,080 --> 00:26:24,540
Ah, gotcha.

295
00:26:24,620 --> 00:26:28,000
Don't mind me, I'm just toasting the happy couple.

296
00:26:28,090 --> 00:26:30,550
On the house!

297
00:26:37,180 --> 00:26:38,970
Anyway.

298
00:26:50,400 --> 00:26:53,320
Don't think that's gonna stop me.

299
00:26:55,990 --> 00:26:58,240
Everyone out! Out now!

300
00:27:02,160 --> 00:27:05,370
Get out, get out, get out!

301
00:27:26,350 --> 00:27:29,230
Open the gate! Use that tube thing, come on!

302
00:27:29,310 --> 00:27:31,650
Sonic screwdriver. - Use it!

303
00:27:31,730 --> 00:27:34,740
Nah. Tell you what, let's go in here.

304
00:27:40,200 --> 00:27:43,120
You can't hide inside a wooden box!

305
00:27:47,250 --> 00:27:49,290
It's going to get us!

306
00:27:50,830 --> 00:27:52,250
Doctor!

307
00:28:18,820 --> 00:28:20,160
It's gonna follow us!

308
00:28:20,240 --> 00:28:22,910
The assembled hordes of Genghis Khan couldn't get through that door.

309
00:28:22,990 --> 00:28:26,580
Believe me, they've tried. Now, shut up a minute.

310
00:28:35,130 --> 00:28:40,260
You see, the arm was too simple. But a head is perfect.

311
00:28:40,340 --> 00:28:44,720
I can use it to trace the signal back to the original source.

312
00:28:45,680 --> 00:28:47,850
Right. Where do you want to start?

313
00:28:47,930 --> 00:28:49,270
Um...

314
00:28:49,350 --> 00:28:51,520
The inside's bigger than the outside?

315
00:28:51,600 --> 00:28:53,690
Yes. - It's... It's alien.

316
00:28:54,060 --> 00:28:55,110
Yep.

317
00:28:56,570 --> 00:28:58,570
Are you alien?

318
00:28:58,650 --> 00:29:01,110
Yes.

319
00:29:01,200 --> 00:29:03,320
Is that all right? - Yeah.

320
00:29:03,410 --> 00:29:06,330
It's called the Tardis, this thing. T-A-R-D-I-S.

321
00:29:06,410 --> 00:29:09,660
That's Time And Relative Dimension In Space.

322
00:29:11,120 --> 00:29:14,290
That's OK. Culture shock. Happens to the best of us.

323
00:29:14,380 --> 00:29:16,840
Did they kill him? Mickey?

324
00:29:16,920 --> 00:29:19,210
Did... Did they kill Mickey? Is he dead?

325
00:29:19,300 --> 00:29:21,720
Oh, I didn't think of that.

326
00:29:21,800 --> 00:29:25,970
He's my boyfriend. You pulled off his head, they copied him,

327
00:29:26,050 --> 00:29:27,640
and you didn't even think?

328
00:29:27,720 --> 00:29:30,310
And now you're just gonna let him melt? - Melt?

329
00:29:32,900 --> 00:29:35,440
Oh, no, no, no, no, no!

330
00:29:35,520 --> 00:29:39,530
What are you doing? - Following the signal. It's fading!

331
00:29:42,740 --> 00:29:45,240
No, no, no, no, no, no, no!

332
00:29:46,780 --> 00:29:49,450
Almost there, almost there...

333
00:29:49,540 --> 00:29:51,750
Here we go!

334
00:29:54,920 --> 00:29:58,420
You can't go out there. It's not safe!

335
00:30:01,380 --> 00:30:04,300
I lost the signal. I got so close!

336
00:30:06,220 --> 00:30:08,430
We've moved. Does it fly?

337
00:30:08,510 --> 00:30:11,060
It disappears there and reappears here. You wouldn't understand.

338
00:30:11,140 --> 00:30:14,140
But if we're... Somewhere else, what about that headless thing?

339
00:30:14,230 --> 00:30:15,150
It's still on the loose.

340
00:30:15,230 --> 00:30:18,440
Melted with the head. Are you going to witter on all night?

341
00:30:18,520 --> 00:30:20,940
I'll have to tell his mother.

342
00:30:23,490 --> 00:30:24,660
Mickey.

343
00:30:24,740 --> 00:30:29,120
I'll have to tell his mother he's dead and you just went and forgot him. Again!

344
00:30:29,200 --> 00:30:30,740
You were right. You are alien.

345
00:30:30,830 --> 00:30:33,660
Look, if I did forget some kid called Mickey- - He's not a kid!

346
00:30:33,750 --> 00:30:36,670
It's because I'm busy trying to save the life of every stupid ape

347
00:30:36,750 --> 00:30:38,790
blundering about on top of this planet, all right?

348
00:30:38,880 --> 00:30:40,500
All right? - Yes, it is!

349
00:30:42,710 --> 00:30:45,050
If you are an alien, how comes you sound like you're from the north?

350
00:30:45,130 --> 00:30:47,140
Lots of planets have a north!

351
00:30:49,810 --> 00:30:52,680
What's a police public call box?

352
00:30:54,180 --> 00:30:58,480
It's a telephone box from the 1950s. It's a disguise.

353
00:30:59,980 --> 00:31:00,980
Okay.

354
00:31:01,070 --> 00:31:04,030
And this... This living plastic, what's it got against us?

355
00:31:04,110 --> 00:31:07,820
Nothing. It loves you. You've got such a good planet. Lots of smoke and oil,

356
00:31:07,910 --> 00:31:11,240
plenty of toxins and dioxins in the air, perfect.

357
00:31:11,330 --> 00:31:13,450
Just what the Nestene Consciousness needs.

358
00:31:13,540 --> 00:31:16,830
Its food stock was destroyed in the war, all its protein planets rotted.

359
00:31:16,920 --> 00:31:20,670
So, Earth? Dinner. - Any way of stopping it?

360
00:31:20,750 --> 00:31:22,050
Antiplastic.

361
00:31:22,130 --> 00:31:24,760
Antiplastic? - Antiplastic!

362
00:31:24,840 --> 00:31:26,090
But first, I've got to find it.

363
00:31:26,170 --> 00:31:28,720
How can you hide something that big in a city this small?

364
00:31:28,800 --> 00:31:31,390
Hold on, hide what? - A transmitter.

365
00:31:31,470 --> 00:31:34,390
The Consciousness is controlling every single piece of plastic,

366
00:31:34,470 --> 00:31:36,480
so it needs a transmitter boosts the signal.

367
00:31:36,560 --> 00:31:38,270
What does it look like? - Like a transmitter.

368
00:31:38,350 --> 00:31:42,110
Round and massive. Somewhere slap bang in the middle of London.

369
00:31:42,190 --> 00:31:46,650
A huge, metal, circular structure, like a dish, like a wheel, radial.

370
00:31:46,740 --> 00:31:50,450
Close to where we're standing! It must be completely invisible.

371
00:31:50,530 --> 00:31:52,120
What?

372
00:31:54,330 --> 00:31:55,950
What?

373
00:31:58,040 --> 00:32:00,130
What is it? What?

374
00:32:03,460 --> 00:32:05,090
Oh.

375
00:32:06,720 --> 00:32:08,760
Fantastic!

376
00:32:29,990 --> 00:32:34,870
Think of it. Plastic. All over the world, every artificial thing waiting to come alive.

377
00:32:34,950 --> 00:32:37,660
The shop window dummies, the phones, the wires, the cables.

378
00:32:37,750 --> 00:32:40,960
The breast implants. - Still, we've found the transmitter.

379
00:32:41,040 --> 00:32:44,000
The Consciousness must be somewhere underneath.

380
00:32:46,590 --> 00:32:49,130
What about down here?

381
00:32:52,050 --> 00:32:54,100
Looks good to me.

382
00:33:37,850 --> 00:33:39,680
The Nestene Consciousness.

383
00:33:39,770 --> 00:33:43,060
That's it, inside the vat. A living, plastic creature.

384
00:33:43,150 --> 00:33:46,020
Well then, tip in your antiplastic and let's go.

385
00:33:46,110 --> 00:33:49,990
I'm not here to kill it. I've got to give it a chance.

386
00:33:56,450 --> 00:34:00,790
I seek audience with the Nestene Consciousness under peaceful contract

387
00:34:00,870 --> 00:34:04,670
according to Convention 15 of the Shadow Proclamation.

388
00:34:07,000 --> 00:34:10,710
Thank you. If I might have permission to approach?

389
00:34:13,010 --> 00:34:15,010
Oh my God.

390
00:34:16,800 --> 00:34:19,810
Mickey! It's me! It's OK.

391
00:34:19,890 --> 00:34:23,230
It's all right. - That thing down there...

392
00:34:23,310 --> 00:34:26,810
The liquid, Rose, it can talk! - Oh, you're stinking!

393
00:34:26,900 --> 00:34:28,320
Doctor, they kept him alive!

394
00:34:28,400 --> 00:34:32,400
Yeah, that was always a possibility. Keep him alive to maintain the copy.

395
00:34:32,490 --> 00:34:37,200
You knew that and you never said? - Can we keep domestics outside, thank you.

396
00:34:49,380 --> 00:34:51,840
Am I addressing the Consciousness?

397
00:34:53,340 --> 00:34:55,380
Thank you. If I might observe,

398
00:34:55,470 --> 00:34:59,640
you infiltrated this civilisation by means of warp shunt technology.

399
00:34:59,720 --> 00:35:03,100
So, may I suggest with the greatest respect, that you shunt off?!

400
00:35:05,520 --> 00:35:08,310
Oh, don't give me that! It's an invasion, plain and simple.

401
00:35:08,400 --> 00:35:10,650
Don't talk about constitutional rights.

402
00:35:13,030 --> 00:35:15,570
I am talking!

403
00:35:17,820 --> 00:35:21,120
This planet is just starting. These stupid, little people

404
00:35:21,200 --> 00:35:24,910
have only just learnt how to walk but hey are capable of so much more.

405
00:35:25,000 --> 00:35:28,460
I'm asking you, on their behalf. Please just go.

406
00:35:28,540 --> 00:35:30,090
Doctor!

407
00:35:35,920 --> 00:35:38,890
That was just insurance, I wasn't gonna use it.

408
00:35:41,180 --> 00:35:44,390
I was not attacking you, I'm here to help. I'm not your enemy.

409
00:35:44,470 --> 00:35:45,890
I swear, I'm not.

410
00:35:48,850 --> 00:35:50,860
What do you mean?

411
00:35:50,940 --> 00:35:53,650
No. Oh, no. Honestly, no!

412
00:35:54,360 --> 00:35:56,110
Yes, that's my ship.

413
00:35:59,410 --> 00:36:01,700
That's not true! I should know, I was there.

414
00:36:01,780 --> 00:36:04,120
I fought in the war. It wasn't my fault!

415
00:36:04,870 --> 00:36:08,330
I couldn't save your world, I couldn't save any of them!

416
00:36:09,960 --> 00:36:11,790
What's it doing? - It's the Tardis!

417
00:36:12,380 --> 00:36:16,210
The Nestene's identified it as superior technology. It's terrified!

418
00:36:16,300 --> 00:36:18,550
It's going to the final base.

419
00:36:18,630 --> 00:36:23,100
It's starting the invasion. Get out, Rose! Just leg it! Now!

420
00:36:24,970 --> 00:36:25,720
Mum?

421
00:36:25,810 --> 00:36:28,060
Oh, there you are. I was just gonna phone.

422
00:36:28,140 --> 00:36:30,600
You can get compensation, I've said so.

423
00:36:30,690 --> 00:36:33,230
I've got this document thing off the police. Don't thank me!

424
00:36:33,320 --> 00:36:36,030
Where are you, Mum? - I'm in town.

425
00:36:36,110 --> 00:36:38,280
No, go home! Just go home right now.

426
00:36:38,360 --> 00:36:41,740
Darling, you're breaking up. Listen, I'm just gonna do a bit of late-night shopping.

427
00:36:41,820 --> 00:36:43,910
I'll see you later. Ta-ra!

428
00:36:43,990 --> 00:36:45,790
Mum! Mum?

429
00:36:51,750 --> 00:36:55,840
It's the activation signal! It's transmitting!

430
00:37:01,260 --> 00:37:03,470
It's the end of the world.

431
00:37:11,850 --> 00:37:13,190
There's no point in creating a spreadsheet

432
00:37:13,270 --> 00:37:15,520
if you're going to spend summer money in winter months!

433
00:37:15,610 --> 00:37:18,530
Oh my God! I thought they were dummies.

434
00:37:18,610 --> 00:37:20,820
I nearly had a heart attack!

435
00:37:47,390 --> 00:37:52,060
It's true. Everything I've read, all the stories, it's all true!

436
00:37:59,780 --> 00:38:03,610
Get out, Rose! Just get out! Run!

437
00:38:03,700 --> 00:38:06,120
The stairs have gone!

438
00:38:10,500 --> 00:38:12,910
I haven't got a key!

439
00:38:14,960 --> 00:38:17,000
We're gonna die!

440
00:39:39,580 --> 00:39:41,710
Just leave him!

441
00:39:48,050 --> 00:39:50,260
There's nothing you can do!

442
00:39:51,050 --> 00:39:53,680
I've got no A-levels,

443
00:39:53,770 --> 00:39:55,270
no job,

444
00:39:55,350 --> 00:39:57,560
no future,

445
00:39:57,640 --> 00:39:59,980
but I'll tell you what I have got.

446
00:40:00,060 --> 00:40:04,190
Jericho Street Junior School Under-7s Gymnastic Team.

447
00:40:04,280 --> 00:40:06,400
I've got the bronze!

448
00:40:19,830 --> 00:40:21,420
Rose!

449
00:40:24,630 --> 00:40:26,970
Now we're in trouble!

450
00:42:05,360 --> 00:42:09,190
Rose! Rose, don't go out of the house. It's not safe!

451
00:42:09,280 --> 00:42:12,360
There were these things and they were shooting and-

452
00:42:12,450 --> 00:42:14,240
Hello?

453
00:42:19,160 --> 00:42:21,500
Fat lot of good you were!

454
00:42:23,750 --> 00:42:26,750
Nestene Consciousness? Easy.

455
00:42:26,830 --> 00:42:29,920
You were useless in there! You'd be dead if it wasn't for me.

456
00:42:30,000 --> 00:42:31,260
Yes, I would.

457
00:42:32,170 --> 00:42:33,680
Thank you.

458
00:42:34,220 --> 00:42:36,300
Right, then! I'll be off.

459
00:42:36,890 --> 00:42:39,100
Unless, uh... I don't know,

460
00:42:39,760 --> 00:42:42,020
You could come with me.

461
00:42:42,600 --> 00:42:44,270
This box isn't just a London hopper, you know.

462
00:42:44,350 --> 00:42:46,600
It goes anywhere in the universe. Free of charge!

463
00:42:46,690 --> 00:42:47,810
Don't!

464
00:42:48,060 --> 00:42:50,070
He's an alien. He's a... Thing!

465
00:42:50,150 --> 00:42:52,440
He's not invited.

466
00:42:52,990 --> 00:42:54,610
What do you think?

467
00:42:55,860 --> 00:42:59,490
You could stay here. Fill your life with work and food and sleep,

468
00:42:59,580 --> 00:43:01,120
or you could go...

469
00:43:01,950 --> 00:43:03,660
Anywhere.

470
00:43:03,750 --> 00:43:06,330
Is it always this dangerous? - Yeah.

471
00:43:07,830 --> 00:43:10,460
Yeah, I can't. I have, um...

472
00:43:10,550 --> 00:43:13,380
I've got to go and find my mum and...

473
00:43:13,460 --> 00:43:16,800
Someone's got to look after this stupid lump. So...

474
00:43:18,970 --> 00:43:20,430
Okay.

475
00:43:21,430 --> 00:43:23,220
See you around.

476
00:43:56,840 --> 00:43:58,590
Come on, let's go.

477
00:44:18,320 --> 00:44:22,330
By the way, did I mention it also travels in time?

478
00:44:26,660 --> 00:44:29,540
Thanks. - Thanks for what?

479
00:44:29,620 --> 00:44:31,500
Exactly.

480
00:44:43,180 --> 00:44:45,720
This is the year five billion.

481
00:44:45,810 --> 00:44:49,600
And this is the day... Hold on...

482
00:44:51,400 --> 00:44:54,440
Welcome to the end of the world.

483
00:44:54,520 --> 00:44:57,820
Who the hell are you? - Oh, I'm The Doctor. This is Rose Tyler.

484
00:44:57,900 --> 00:44:59,700
She's my plus one. Is that all right?

485
00:44:59,780 --> 00:45:06,120
Representing the Forest of Cheam, we have Trees. The Moxx of Balhoon.

486
00:45:06,200 --> 00:45:12,830
The Face of Boe. The last human. The Lady Cassandra O'Brien.

487
00:45:12,920 --> 00:45:16,590
Oh, now, don't stare. Look how thin I am.

488
00:45:19,590 --> 00:45:21,220
That's not supposed to happen.

1
